[Site "https://lichess.org/analysis/r1bqkbnr/1ppp1ppp/p1n5/1B2p3/4P3/5N2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R_w_KQkq_-_0_4"]
[Role "exercise"]

{ You asked the question. Now see how he answers it. }
4. Ba4 { He does not take: he slides back and keeps aiming at your knight. Which piece is still asleep? [%csl Ra4] } 4... Nf6 { That one. Out it comes, poking his e pawn on the way past. [%cal Gf6e4] } (4... b5 { You may chase the bishop at once. It costs a little time. } 5. Bb3 Nf6 { Fine. We land in the same place anyway. }) (4... Bc5 { A perfectly good square for the bishop. } 5. c3 Nf6 { The same knight move, one beat later. }) (4... d6 { Solid and slow, and your dark bishop is shut in again. } 5. O-O b5 { Playable, and he is very comfortable. }) (4... Be7 { Safe there, and rather sleepy. } 5. O-O b5 { You are fine, just very quiet. }) 5. O-O { He castles, and his e pawn looks free. Careful: is it really? } 5... Be7 { Calm and correct. The bishop steps out and your king can go home next. } (5... Nxe4 { You may take it. That is the open Spanish, and it gets sharp very fast. } 6. d4 Be7 7. Re1 { A real line, and an awful lot to remember. }) (5... b5 { Chasing him first is perfectly good too. } 6. Bb3 Bb7 { Fine chess, and the bishop comes out next anyway. }) (5... d6 { Safe, slow, and a little sad for your dark bishop. } 6. Re1 b5 { He is a touch better and your bishop is still at home. }) (5... Bc5 { An active square, and it walks straight into a pawn push. } 6. c3 O-O 7. d4 { He gains time on the bishop and takes the whole middle. }) 6. Re1 { The rook joins in, and now your e pawn really is hanging. Do not castle yet. [%csl Re5] } 6... b5 { The pawn shoves the bishop away first, so the trade on c6 wins him nothing. [%cal Gb5a4] } (6... O-O { The natural move, and here it simply drops the pawn. } 7. Bxc6 bxc6 8. Nxe5 { Your d pawn blocks the queen again, so there is no fork, and e5 is gone. }) (6... d6 { Solid, and it guards the pawn. Almost as good as ours. } 7. c3 O-O { A fine game. Shoving the bishop first asks more questions. }) (6... Bc5 { The bishop steps out, and the pawn is still loose. } 7. c3 b5 { You have to play the pawn move anyway. }) (6... Nd4 { A tempting jump, and he trades it off with time to spare. } 7. Nxd4 exd4 8. c3 { His pawns roll forward and you are worse. }) 0-1


[Event "Black openings: the Scotch centre push"]
[Result "0-1"]
[Variant "Standard"]
